<title>FRANCE: France has not yet decided on taxing stock options.</title>
<headline>France has not yet decided on taxing stock options.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government has not yet taken a decision whether to agree or not with a proposal from a Senate commission to submit stock options to the CSG social security levy, the Prime Minister's office said.</p>
<p>On Thursday morning, the social affairs commission of parliament's upper house adapted unanimously voted an amendment to the draft bill on financing the social security system with the aim of submitting earnings from stock options to the CSG.</p>
<p>Stock options are options to buy a company's stock on relatively advantageous terms issued to company executives as an incentive to boost the company's share performance.</p>
</text>
